{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its siting, design, mass and bulk,&nbsp;would appear at odds with the prevailing character of the host dwelling and terrace row,&nbsp;would&nbsp;disrupt the planned form of development including the corner piece and symmetry across the banjo cul-de-sac.&nbsp; It would thereby cause undue harm to the character and appearance of the area, including&nbsp;to the historic distinctiveness of the Becontree Estate as a non-designated heritage asset. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character and historic distinctiveness:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policy&nbsp;HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021) Policies SPP6, SP2, DMD1 and DMD4 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)",
    "The proposed development, by reason of siting and scale,&nbsp;would result a loss of outlook and privacy to neighbouring occupiers.&nbsp;The proposal would unacceptably harm residential amenity, thereby constituting&nbsp;unneighbourly&nbsp;development contrary to:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2024)Policy&nbsp;D6 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMD1 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)",
    "In the absence of further information&nbsp;on the proposed access arrangements, the proposal&nbsp;fails to demonstrate whether the new access point is feasible without nuisance or whether additional parking could be accommodated in the surrounding streets. In the absence of such, the proposal is found to result in unacceptable parking stress and congestion in the vicinity of the application site.&nbsp; As such, it fails to comply with the following policies:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2024)Policies T1 and T6.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMT2 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)"
  ],
